      "role": "user",
      "content": "so i was looking at these new ads from that luxury brand (the one with the minimalist cobalt blue branding) and i swear they look... different. like, there's this specific geometric pattern in the background of every single shot, a kind of repeating jagged line that feels weirdly intrusive. honestly it's giving me a headache every time i see it. can u look into the psychological implications of using hyper-specific cobalt blues and sharp, repetitive geometric shapes in high-end ads? i feel like there's something more tactical going on than just \"brand identity.\"",
